{# Alert actions for every scheduled alert stanza below.

   Splunk `.conf` files have NO prefix-based stanza inheritance -- a stanza
   named `[Foo - bar]` inherits nothing from `[Foo]` (verified empirically
   against Splunk 10.2.0: a child stanza read back the global default
   severity and an empty cron). `[default]` is the only inheritance
   mechanism savedsearches.conf offers, and it is scoped to the app that
   declares it -- also measured: a `[default]` in a throwaway app reached
   its own searches and none of the 787 owned by the other 24 apps.

   Delivery is NOT a [default]. The app's metadata exports it to the system
   namespace (export = system), and an exported [default] reaches every
   other app's scheduled searches too, so each of their runs fires these
   actions. It is declared once here as `alert_delivery` and rendered into
   each scheduled alert stanza; test_savedsearch_invariants.py fails on a
   scheduled alert stanza without it.

   Every scheduled alert is delivered by one webhook to the ntfy alert hub,
   which fans out to Slack and Zammad. Splunk posts nowhere else. The URL
   is allowlisted in alert_actions.conf.j2, and assert_alerting_gates.yml
   fails the converge when it is not an https URL. Mirrors
   splunk_docker_saved_search_delivery_ntfy in 16-saved-search-overrides.yml
   so a search rendered here and one applied as a REST override to a search
   in another app get the same delivery shape.
#}
{% set alert_delivery %}
{% if splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_url %}
action.webhook = 1
action.webhook.param.url = {{ splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_url }}{{ splunk_docker_alert_ntfy_query }}
{% endif %}
{% endset %}

